# Project docs (dhara_storage)

When creating or editing README / AGENTS / `docs/` in this repo, **read and follow the `project-docs` skill first**, then apply the customizations below.

Source **documentation comments**, file headers, and why-comments → global skill **`inline-code-docs`** (not this rule).

## DROT ownership (do not duplicate)

Operator tool docs, AGENTS, and Cursor rules live in the **`tooling/drot` submodule**:

| Surface | Location |
|---------|----------|
| DROT AGENTS | [`tooling/drot/AGENTS.md`](../../tooling/drot/AGENTS.md) |
| DROT docs | [`tooling/drot/docs/`](../../tooling/drot/docs/) |
| DROT project-docs rule | [`tooling/drot/.cursor/rules/project-docs.mdc`](../../tooling/drot/.cursor/rules/project-docs.mdc) |
| DROT logging rule | [`tooling/drot/.cursor/rules/logging.mdc`](../../tooling/drot/.cursor/rules/logging.mdc) |

When editing DROT behavior or operator logging/TUI docs, change files **under `tooling/drot/`**. Storage `docs/` may keep short redirect stubs only.

## Product intent

Pitch, exclusions, and design lineage: **[AGENTS.md → Product intent](../../AGENTS.md)**. Do not invent a new product story. Do not put Windows.Storage name-drops or war stories in READMEs.

